From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_SCALED_ONLY review fixes: keep the native copy when the scaled one has no memory; no "Missing image" line for a freed copy

What: Image::CanReleaseNative (vk_texture_cache.cpp) also refuses an image whose scaled copy is
missing or unbacked (MemoryAllocator::CreateImage's out-of-memory fallback: an image with nothing
bound keeps no data). Image::DownloadMemory no longer writes its LOG_CRITICAL "Missing image at
download" line for an image whose native copy 0810 freed (ScaleDown makes it again right after).
Why: review of 0810. Freeing the native copy of an image whose scaled copy has no memory would lose
the picture for good (without the switch it stays in the native copy). And every download of a
freed image wrote a critical log line that log readers count as a fault.
Off: nothing new runs (both tests sit behind native_released / ReleaseNative's switch test).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
index 44872cbd8e..653fb21d92 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -3892,7 +3892,8 @@ void Image::DownloadMemory(VkBuffer buffer, size_t offset,
 
 void Image::DownloadMemory(std::span<VkBuffer> buffers_span, std::span<size_t> offsets_span,
                             std::span<const VideoCommon::BufferImageCopy> copies) {
-    if (!original_image) {
+    // EDEN_UP_SCALED_ONLY: a freed native copy is not missing; ScaleDown below makes it again.
+    if (!original_image && !native_released) {
         LOG_CRITICAL(Render_Vulkan, "Missing image at download: gpu={:#x}, cpu={:#x}, type={}, format={}, flags={:#x}, size={}, dimensions={}x{}",
                      gpu_addr, cpu_addr, static_cast<u32>(info.type), static_cast<u32>(info.format),
                      static_cast<u32>(flags), unswizzled_size_bytes, info.size.width, info.size.height);
@@ -4872,7 +4873,10 @@ bool Image::CanReleaseNative() const {
                                       ImageFlagBits::TrimmedLevels | ImageFlagBits::CostlyLoad;
     if (info.type != ImageType::e2D || info.num_samples != 1 || host_level_offset != 0 ||
         True(flags & special) || IsPixelFormatASTC(info.format) ||
-        VideoCore::Surface::IsPixelFormatBCn(info.format) || original_image.IsUnbacked()) {
+        VideoCore::Surface::IsPixelFormatBCn(info.format) || original_image.IsUnbacked() ||
+        !scaled_image || scaled_image.IsUnbacked()) {
+        // A scaled copy made with nothing bound (out of memory) keeps no data: the native copy
+        // is then the only one that holds the picture.
         return false;
     }
     const auto has_view = [](const vk::ImageView& view) { return static_cast<bool>(view); };
